      "rationale": "Reviewed, accepted for contact-evidence-4.4 (ADJ-VG-05). The sasebo 52019 estimate lands 144ms early because e09's occlusion-gap censoring (gapCensorMs 150) attenuates the only true-location ball direction-change kernel to 0.3x mass (sparse ORACLE ball annotation: 500ms gap after the turn sample at 52053), so the posterior mode drifts to wrist-speed-peak + ball-wrist-proximity evidence at 51875. f09 (contact-evidence-4.3, f76f95ef) fixed the confidence side of this row — censoring can no longer raise confidence, 0.792 → 0.683, below the 0.7 confirm band, and the row carries no_paddle_evidence — and deliberately did not move the estimate: relaxing gap censoring re-opens the e09 confident-wrong attacks it closes, and retuning to a single sparse-oracle gold row is not defensible (see datasets/experiments/wave-f/f09-contact-adversarial-fixes-summary.json). g02 measured the same row under oracle ownership and found it unchanged: downstream contact-evidence localization error, not ownership error (datasets/experiments/wave-g/g02-f09-oracle-summary.json). The faead-feed 33688 row is the same censoring change turning an abstention into a low-confidence acceptable estimate (coverage +0.1). Together they move medianErrorMs 17 → 27, p75 25 → 110, p90 65 → 128 on n=7 estimated target events. contact-evidence-4.4 (h26 red-team fixes) leaves every e02 target row identical to 4.3. Ceilings are pinned at the measured values: wrongMarkers 1, medianErrorMs 27 — any further regression fails the gate.",
      "introducedBy": "contact-evidence-4.3 (f76f95ef0ddddfbb4556746b8e5099a27a83eada, f09) — the e09 occlusion-gap censoring merged with e02 on parallel branches",
